{
  "_about": [
    "Worked cases for a TARGET's `skip` text (spec 2026-09-23 flows mosaic, 3.1 and 3.2): what compile.parse_skip reads out of it on a grid of `rows` x `cols`.",
    "`skip` is the 1-based [row, col] pairs, each panel once, in grid order; `unread` is every entry that names no panel of this grid, in the order typed.",
    "Graded twice against this one file: server/tests/test_flows_skip_fixture.py against parse_skip itself, and ui/src/components/flows/framing/__tests__/framingModel.test.ts against the modal's mirror (framingModel.ts parseSkip). A case added here is graded on both sides on the next run. Do not copy it into either test.",
    "The whitespace and digit cases are there because Python's str.strip(), `\\s` and `\\d` are Unicode-wide and JavaScript's trim() and `\\d` are not the same sets: a mirror written with the JS defaults reads a fullwidth '\uff13-1' as nothing (the run would skip a panel the modal draws as live) and strips a BOM the server keeps.",
    "The digit-run cases are #441's: past CPython's integer string limit (4300 digits, leading zeros counted) int() raises, so parse_skip reads such an entry as unread, as it reads a row past the last, and the mirror's pyInt counts the digits the same way. A run of exactly 4300 digits is read."
  ],
